From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@tuta.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:49:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: s5kjn1: Reject mode changes while streaming

An active format request can select a different mode while streaming.
The driver changes the reported geometry and timing controls but the
sensor continues sending frames according to the old mode registers.

Return -EBUSY for active format requests that change the streaming mode.
Still allow TRY requests and requests for the current mode.

Fixes: e38fd0933c75 ("media: i2c: add Samsung S5KJN1 image sensor device driver")
Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@tuta.io>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c b/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c
index a4255fbd9..4fb5fc646 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c
@@ -1038,6 +1038,9 @@ static int s5kjn1_set_pad_format(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 	if (fmt->which == V4L2_SUBDEV_FORMAT_TRY || s5kjn1->mode == mode)
 		goto set_format;
 
+	if (v4l2_subdev_is_streaming(sd))
+		return -EBUSY;
+
 	/* Update limits and set FPS and exposure to default values */
 	hblank = mode->hts - mode->width;
 	__v4l2_ctrl_modify_range(s5kjn1->hblank, hblank, hblank, 1, hblank);
